  "pd": {
    "basis": "author-died-pre-1930",
    "detail": "Antonin Dvorak died in 1904. Symphony No. 9 Op. 95 was written in New York in 1893 and published by Simrock in 1894, so the composition is free worldwide.",
    "sourceEdition": "Dvorak, Symphony No. 9 Op. 95, second movement Largo, the cor anglais theme checked note-for-note against a public-domain melodic transcription of the orchestral score in the original key of D flat major, 4/4",
    "notes": "Dvorak melody and harmony only; this is the orchestral Largo theme, not the Fisher song arrangement. The words William Arms Fisher set to this theme in 1922 are carried on the Theme A section under their own separate lyrics.pd block - they are public domain in their own right (US publication 1922), which is checked independently of Dvorak's dates."
  },
