  ],
  "feel": "straight",
  "confidence": "high",
  "notes": "A real ABA form. Theme A is the pentatonic cor anglais tune; the dotted figure is what makes it recognisable, so it is written exactly. Theme B is the relative-minor middle strain, stated twice, forte then piano as the score marks it. The reprise climbs an octave for the climax before the tag fades out. NOTE ON NOTATION: the tune is encoded in half time -- every note value is doubled (the score's dotted eighth plus sixteenth is written here as a dotted quarter plus eighth), so one bar of the score becomes two bars here and the bar-granular chords can follow the harmony. tempoBPM is therefore 104, double the score's Largo quarter = 52; the two cancel out and the theme sounds at its proper Largo speed. The closing harp and flute arpeggio of the movement is built on triplets and is deliberately not encoded. Kept in the original D flat; transpose in the app if the key is awkward.",
